temp/
# Planning documents are working artifacts and are never committed — including
# the cross-repo ones. They are written here and read from a sibling checkout by
# relative path (../aitp-control-plane/plans/cross-repo/...), which needs no
# blob URL. An issue in another repo that wants the content should quote it
# rather than link to it.
plans/

# /drive process artifacts. Same rule as plans/ above: working documents, never
# committed. These were untracked but NOT ignored, so a `git add -A` swept them
# into PRs (DECISIONS.md O2). Anything here that must outlive a session gets
# promoted deliberately — to an issue, a PR body, or an inline code comment
# next to the thing it explains (see package.json's `//overrides` key and the
# comment blocks in next.config.ts).
PROGRESS.md
ASSUMPTIONS.md
DECISIONS.md
.drive.lock
